# Local development secrets for `pnpm dev:registry`. Copy to `.dev.vars`, which is gitignored.
#
#   cp apps/registry/.dev.vars.example apps/registry/.dev.vars
#
# These are NOT the production values and must never be. Production secrets are generated by
# Terraform and pushed with `wrangler secret bulk` (ADR-0040, docs/OPERATIONS.md § Secrets).
#
# Without this file the Worker starts, `GET /v1/health` answers 200, and **every `/v1/nodes` request
# fails with a logged `INTERNAL`** — `src/env.ts` refuses rather than handing an empty key to WebCrypto,
# which rejects it anyway. That is the least diagnosable shape a misconfiguration takes, and it is why
# `scripts/dev-preflight.mjs` creates this file rather than leaving it to be discovered.

# Signs proof-of-work challenges for `POST /v1/nodes`.
#
# **Deliberately a different value from `apps/node/.dev.vars`'s `POW_SECRET`**, and the difference is the
# point rather than hygiene: both services issue and verify challenges with the same algorithm, so a
# shared key would make a challenge issued by the node redeemable at the registry. Enrolling a node into
# the directory would then be gated by whatever the cheapest tunnel create in the world costs. Terraform
# keeps two independent `random_password` resources for exactly this, and `pnpm deploy:check` fails if
# they ever come from one.
POW_SECRET="local-development-registry-pow-secret-not-for-production"
